[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163] STEP PURPOSE
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   step_163: forward-modelled discovery footprint for the arrival anisotropy (b129).
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   Step 152 (b116) conditioned the arrival-direction null on the observed
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   latitude marginals and left an explicit caveat: the second-order bias --
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   longitude structure produced by opposition-pointing and survey geometry --
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   was not modelled.  A later diagnostic (longitude-permutation null) showed
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   that conditioning on the observed longitude marginal removes the cap
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   excess, but that null is not decisive: a marginal-level dipole signal is
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   absorbed into the conditioned marginal by construction.  The decisive
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   question is whether a physically modelled discovery footprint can produce
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   the observed aphelion-direction dipole in the first place.
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   This step builds that footprint as a forward model.  For each real comet
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   the orbit shape (q, e) and perihelion epoch are kept fixed while the
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   spatial orientation is redrawn isotropically (Haar-random rotations of
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   the perifocal frame).  Each orientation is propagated over its bright
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   window (r < r_vis, Barker Kepler conic time law) and scored by whether the
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   geocentric position is in the night sky (solar elongation > el_min), in
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   the declination reach of the historical northern-observatory record
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   (dec > dec_min), and within geocentric distance dmax.  Discovery weight
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   is the observable brightness integral sum dt/(r^2 Delta^2).  The pooled
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   weight map on the (randomised) aphelion directions is the predicted
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   discovered-population marginal under an isotropic source.
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   Tests
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   T1  footprint dipole vs observed dipole: predicted direction and
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   amplitude of the discovered-population aphelion dipole under an
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   isotropic source, and its angular separation from the observed
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   dipole.
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   T2  selection-only null: n arrival directions are resampled from the
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   brightness-weighted footprint pool; the distribution of the
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   resulting dipole direction relative to the declared transit axis
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   gives p_dir = P(sep <= observed) and p_joint = P(R >= observed
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   and sep <= observed).  The in-cap fraction under the same null
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   prices the cap statistic against the footprint.
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   T3  dipole decomposition: the observed mean direction vector is fit
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   as A*(transit axis) + B*(footprint direction); the displaced
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   control axis (120,-40) is fit in parallel as a specificity check.
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   T4  robustness: the footprint dipole and the residual's axis
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   separation are recomputed over a grid of window depths,
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   elongation limits, declination limits and discovery-weight
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   schemes.
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   T5  longitude-marginal diagnostic: predicted vs observed ecliptic-
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   longitude dipole of the aphelion direction (the channel the
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   latitude-conditioned nulls cannot see).
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   Cohorts: CODE class-1 (all and q < 3.1 matched) and the SBDB
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   near-parabolic lineage cohorts (pre-2018, post-2017, all), using the
[2026-10-16 14:36:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 163]   same membership definitions as steps 124/149/152.
